# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for the sanitizers workflow.
#
# corto (third_party/corto, upstream cnr-isti-vclab/corto) is imported unmodified. It reads and
# writes integers through casted byte pointers at unaligned offsets of its stream buffers
# (cstream.h OutStream::write<T> / InStream::read<T>); its normal predictor
# (NormalAttr::preDelta) casts a normal that is not finite (zero-area or unreferenced geometry)
# to int (normal_attribute.h, "-nan is outside the range of representable values of type 'int'"),
# which gives INT_MIN on x86, so the deltas and the bit-width arithmetic overflow (point.h
# operator-=, cstream.h encodeArray, BitStream::write shifts by 32); and OutStream::push() calls
# memcpy(pos, nullptr, 0) for an empty array.
#
# These entries are temporary: the commit that fixes the code deletes its entry. Nothing else is
# listed, a report anywhere else is a bug to fix.
alignment:corto/
signed-integer-overflow:corto/
shift-exponent:corto/
nonnull-attribute:corto/
float-cast-overflow:corto/include/corto/normal_attribute.h
